                                    <h1>SEO Cost for eCommerce Brands 2026-2027 (India + Global)</h1>
                                    <p>eCommerce SEO is one of the highest-compounding marketing investments — but also one of the slowest. Costs vary widely depending on scope (technical audit vs ongoing content vs link-building). Here are realistic 2026-2027 pricing benchmarks + what actually drives ROI.</p>
                                    <h2>SEO Pricing Bands — India 2026</h2>
                                    <p><strong>SMB / early-stage eCommerce:</strong> ₹40K-1.5 lakh / month.<br><strong>Growth-stage eCommerce:</strong> ₹1.5-5 lakh / month.<br><strong>Enterprise eCommerce (100K+ SKUs, multi-market):</strong> ₹5-25 lakh / month.<br><strong>Technical SEO audit (one-time):</strong> ₹75K-6 lakh depending on site size.<br><strong>Link-building programs:</strong> ₹30K-3 lakh / month depending on link volume + quality.</p>
                                    <h2>SEO Pricing — International Regions</h2>
                                    <p><strong>USA:</strong> $2K-15K / month growth-stage; $15K-60K enterprise.<br><strong>UK:</strong> £1.5K-12K growth; £12K-50K enterprise.<br><strong>UAE:</strong> AED 8K-45K growth; AED 45K-200K enterprise.<br><strong>Australia:</strong> AUD 2K-18K growth; AUD 18K-80K enterprise.</p>
                                    <h2>What eCommerce SEO Actually Includes</h2>
                                    <p>1. <strong>Technical foundation:</strong> Core Web Vitals, indexation, schema, sitemap.<br>2. <strong>Content:</strong> category-level content, buying guides, comparison content, FAQ.<br>3. <strong>Product page optimisation:</strong> titles, meta, alt tags, structured data.<br>4. <strong>Link acquisition:</strong> digital PR, guest posts, editorial links.<br>5. <strong>International SEO:</strong> hreflang, regional content, market-specific keyword research.<br>6. <strong>AI/GEO optimisation:</strong> making content citable by ChatGPT / Perplexity / Google AI Overviews.</p>
                                    <h2>Timeline: What to Expect</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Months 0-3:</strong> Technical foundation + baseline content.<br><strong>Months 3-6:</strong> Content velocity, first ranking improvements on long-tail.<br><strong>Months 6-12:</strong> Compounding traffic growth, rankings on category head-terms.<br><strong>Months 12-24:</strong> Category authority, organic revenue significant share of total.<br>SEO that shows results in month 1 is either capturing existing intent or being fabricated.</p>
                                    <h2>The GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) Layer</h2>
                                    <p>2026 addition: content must be citable by AI search (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Claude). This means structured factual content, clear author attribution, schema.org, citations, and RAG-friendly formatting. Best SEO agencies now include GEO in their pricing.</p>
                                    <h2>What Actually Drives eCommerce SEO ROI</h2>
                                    <p>Content depth on category + product pages, technical excellence (Core Web Vitals, mobile), authority-building (backlinks + brand mentions), and category-education content that captures buyer research intent. Skip any of these and the compound doesn't happen.</p>

